# {PROJECT_NAME} — collaborative AI coding (trackers + CAMS)

Multiple agents (Cursor, Claude Code) and humans share this codebase. **Chat is ephemeral.** Anything the next agent needs must live in local trackers (`tasks.md`, `sprint.md`, `decision.md`) or the **CAMS** semantic memory layer.

The full workflow — lazy loading, token efficiency, git branching (`docs/BRANCHING.md`), sprint workflow (`docs/SPRINT-WORKFLOW.md`), tracker conventions, claim/handoff fields — is defined once in **[AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)**. This rule just guarantees it's always loaded into every Cursor chat; see that file for the actual content.

Cursor-only note: session logs are written as `sessions/YYYY-MM-DD-cursor.md` (see [CURSOR.md](../../CURSOR.md)).
